", "entities": [303, 1409, 960, 254, 1574, 1293], "window": [28296, 66695], "confidence": 0.87, "evidence": [{"trace_id": "step_01", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_03", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_05", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_06", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_12", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_04", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_07", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_08", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_09", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_11", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_13", "role": "confounder_control"}], "narrative": "A single, well-defined time-respecting chain carries influence from 303 to 1293: 303->1409 (t=47090), 1409->960 (47399), 960->254 (47570), 254->1574 (47742), 1574->1293 (47901). All four inter-hop waits (309, 171, 172, 159) are strictly positive and under the 600-unit limit, and each hop is a directed edge that actually fires once in the window (verified for 303->1409, 960->254, 1574->1293). Confounder checks: (a) the path is not an artifact of hub traffic \u2014 every node on the chain has only 3-9 events and near-unique partners in the whole 38k-unit window, and both endpoints have exactly one event in the active 47000-48000 sub-window; (b) it is not an artifact of sheer volume \u2014 only 65 of 8124 events fall in the sub-window carrying the cascade; (c) it is not a static-connectivity artifact \u2014 the reverse direction 1293->303 reaches only 3 nodes and never arrives, and restricting to [28296, 47000] leaves 303 reaching nothing, so the connection is genuinely order-dependent; (d) tightening max_wait to 150 breaks the chain, confirming the result depends on the actual inter-event lags rather than on the graph being trivially connected. The cascade is real but fragile: it is the unique route found, with no redundant alternatives."}, "raw_final_response": "```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_ff72bb61\",\n  \"decision\": \"present\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [303, 1409, 960, 254, 1574, 1293],\n  \"window\": [28296, 66695],\n  \"confidence\": 0.87,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"A single, well-defined time-respecting chain carries influence from 303 to 1293: 303->1409 (t=47090), 1409->960 (47399), 960->254 (47570), 254->1574 (47742), 1574->1293 (47901). All four inter-hop waits (309, 171, 172, 159) are strictly positive and under the 600-unit limit, and each hop is a directed edge that actually fires once in the window (verified for 303->1409, 960->254, 1574->1293). Confounder checks: (a) the path is not an artifact of hub traffic \u2014 every node on the chain has only 3-9 events and near-unique partners in the whole 38k-unit window, and both endpoints have exactly one event in the active 47000-48000 sub-window; (b) it is not an artifact of sheer volume \u2014 only 65 of 8124 events fall in the sub-window carrying the cascade; (c) it is not a static-connectivity artifact \u2014 the reverse direction 1293->303 reaches only 3 nodes and never arrives, and restricting to [28296, 47000] leaves 303 reaching nothing, so the connection is genuinely order-dependent; (d) tightening max_wait to 150 breaks the chain, confirming the result depends on the actual inter-event lags rather than on the graph being trivially connected. The cascade is real but fragile: it is the unique route found, with no redundant alternatives.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 37199, "total_output_tokens": 3134, "total_tokens": 40333, "total_latency_ms": 50108, "llm_calls": 6, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}